From 93e645f95291043b9f86a90ec041642929afa50c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ian <ian.laffey@mail.mcgill.ca>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 16:34:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] AP_NavEKF3: external position bootstrap for AID_NONE ->
 AID_ABSOLUTE

Adds EK3_OPTIONS bit 3 'ExtPosCanBootstrap'. When set:

1. LOCAL_POSITION_NED publishes from boot once SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN
   provides a valid origin, even while the filter is in AID_NONE. The
   reported position is held at the origin by stock AID_NONE constant-
   position fusion. This unblocks companion-computer position sources
   (e.g. visual navigation) that need LPN to come up before they start
   producing their own fixes.

2. MAV_CMD_EXTERNAL_POSITION_ESTIMATE (43003), which currently rejects
   in AID_NONE, is allowed to transition the filter to AID_ABSOLUTE
   when the vehicle is in flight (inFlight=true). The bootstrap path
   refreshes pos/vel/tas timeouts, opens velocity covariance so airspeed
   and sideslip fusion can build velocity from scratch, and sets the
   _has_forced_position flag.

3. setAidingMode() refreshes lastGpsPosPassTime_ms every cycle while
   _has_forced_position is set, preventing attAidLossCritical/posAidLoss-
   Critical from tearing down AID_ABSOLUTE between companion fixes whose
   cadence (e.g. ~20s for a 500m fix interval at 25 m/s) exceeds the
   EKF's posRetryTime_ms.

The bootstrap is gated on inFlight (rather than just !onGround) so that
on-ground compass interference, pitot-cover effects, and pre-arm sensor
states cannot be baked into the bootstrap. The first accepted external
fix happens with the IMU in its flight motion regime.

Default behaviour is unchanged. Setting EK3_OPTIONS bit 3 is required
to enable the new path.

This patch is part of the Theseus Cyclops EKF integration patch set.
